exports[`help > documents sql 1`] = `
"Usage: better-supabase sql <command> [options]

Low-level SQL module commands: lists, adds, syncs, upgrades and prints module files without touching app code, and writes their data migration

Commands
  list     Lists the SQL modules and which ones the project has
  add      Writes module files and their pgTAP tests, and adds the modules to the config
  sync     Writes the files for the modules the config lists and removes the ones it no longer lists
  upgrade  Rewrites module files to this version's SQL, or exits 1 when one is behind with --check
  data     Writes the data migration for blocks in adopt mode
  print    Prints a module's SQL on stdout

Global options
  --cwd <dir>            Project directory
  --config <file>        Config file, relative to --cwd
  --env <name>           Config environment to apply ($env.<name> or $<name>). Defaults to $BETTER_SUPABASE_ENV, then ci when $CI is set
  --json                 Print one JSON document on stdout; errors as Problem Details. On by default in agent mode
  --agent <auto|yes|no>  Agent mode (JSON output, no prompts, consent for destructive work): auto detects a coding agent, yes or no decide. Defaults to $BETTER_SUPABASE_AGENT, then auto
  --confirm <token>      The token from a consent_required result, passed once the user agreed
  -y, --yes              Ask nothing; use the flags and the defaults
  --no-color             Print no colors, like $NO_COLOR
  --debug                Print stack traces, the commands the CLI runs, and timings on stderr
  -h, --help             Show help

Docs: https://bettersupabase.com/docs/blocks/sql
"
`;

